  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 3-2-1 (plane-line-point, CMM-style) work-offset alignment from picks, so a model no longer has to be rotated to fit the WCS.\n\n- `camcraft_app::pick::align_321(world, picks)` (new `crates/app/src/pick/align.rs`) reads the open operation's picks as datums:\n  - exactly one **flat face** → WCS **Z** (its outward normal, from the facets' winding),\n  - exactly one **straight open edge** → **X** (projected into that plane; refused when it stands within 5° of square to the face),\n  - at most one **origin**: a vertex, or a curved face / bore (its centre) - projected onto the face. X runs from the edge end nearer the origin; with no origin pick, the origin is the edge's start.\n  - The frame becomes roll/pitch/yaw (Shepperd matrix → quaternion → `quat_to_euler`), finite-checked.\n- UI: an **Align WCS (3-2-1)** button under the Geometry picks queues the existing undoable `SetWcs` into the WCS pane's slot (`vertex_pick::queue_wcs_321`). It is dark until the picks qualify, with the app's refusal as its tooltip.\n- No new command: `SetWcsOrigin` already carries a rotation.\n- Snapshots `egui_app.png` / `egui_app_light.png` move by the new (dark) button only. **They overlap PR #188's snapshot change** - whichever merges second regenerates them.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#187).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, on 8b3163d)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wcs_align --test face_origin --test vertex_pick --test commands_undo`: green.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: green except `tool_editor_snapshot` (a 4-pixel software-GL diff that also fails on main on this machine).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `wcs_align::a_square_block_aligns_to_the_world_frame`\n- `wcs_align::the_origin_at_the_far_end_turns_x_round`\n- `wcs_align::a_turned_block_aligns_to_its_own_edge_and_the_angles_round_trip` (also places G54 through `SetWcsOrigin`)\n- `wcs_align::a_side_face_tilts_z_and_without_an_origin_the_edge_start_is_used`\n- `wcs_align::every_missing_or_doubled_datum_is_refused_by_name`\n- `egui_app::tests::face_origin::align_wcs_321_places_g54_from_the_face_and_edge_picks` (dark with a face alone; face + edge places G54; undo restores)\n\nChangelog: Align a work offset 3-2-1 from a picked flat face, straight edge and vertex or bore (Align WCS button under the picks)\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork) - feat, merges at the next cut.\n\nFixes #187\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
